# A hook is run by sh, and sh reads the shebang literally. Checked out with CRLF
# on a machine where core.autocrlf is true, `#!/bin/sh` becomes `#!/bin/sh\r` and
# the hook dies with "bad interpreter". The working copy here is already LF, so
# this pins what a fresh clone gets rather than changing anything now.
.githooks/** text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
